              {
                "text": "**Analyzing Task Structures**\n\nI've got a grasp of the two main task patterns. There's a 3x3 colored grid, straightforward enough. But then there's this unusual pattern of 5s. They're arranged in blocks of two, mostly, with zeros interspersed. I'm focusing on how those blocks of 5s are laid out.\n\n\n**Discovering Shape Structure**\n\nI've discovered the single-color shapes are masks composed of k x k blocks! My focus has shifted to determining the specific arrangement within these blocks. I'm noting patterns within the training data, and I've analyzed train 1 to see the relationship of the block structures. Specifically, I'm working on train 2, to determine block structure in the second dataset. Right now I'm attempting to work out block size.\n\n\n",
                "type": "reasoning_text"
              }
            ],
            "encrypted_content": null,
