                "annotations": [],
                "text": "An analysis of the training examples reveals the following rule:\n\n1. The input contains two objects:\n   - A multi-colored pattern of size $H \\times W$.\n   - A larger single-colored shape composed of $k \\times k$ blocks arranged in a grid of dimensions $H \\times W$.\n2. The single-colored block structure forms a binary mask where each $k \\times k$ block of color represents a `1` and empty space within the bounding grid represents a `0`.\n3. The output is obtained by masking the multi-colored pattern with this binary grid (keeping colors where the mask is `1` and replacing with `0` where the mask is `0`).\n\nI am ready for the test input.",
